---
import AcademicLayout from "../../layouts/AcademicLayout.astro";
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<AcademicLayout title="Research & Evidence" currentSection="research">
  <div class="container container-prose page-wrapper">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge-tier e0">RESEARCH INTEGRITY & SCHOLARSHIP</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Research & Evidence</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        Normative whitepaper, research logs, canonical definitions, and verified scientific prior art.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose-content">
      <section id="whitepaper">
        <h2>1. The Dyadic State Whitepaper</h2>
        <p>
          The formal research paper <em>"The Dyadic State: A Framework for Measuring Long-Term Human–Machine Interaction"</em> 
          establishes the complete theoretical motivation, mathematical foundation, and threat analysis for the SYMN-01 benchmark.
        </p>
        <div class="paper-download-card">
          <div>
            <h3>The Dyadic State: Framework & Normative Specification</h3>
            <p>HarVa Groups Research Initiative | v0.1.0 (2026)</p>
          </div>
          <div class="paper-actions">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}/method`} class="btn btn-secondary">Read Online Spec</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/harvatechs/symnoesis/tree/main/spec" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Spec Source</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="evidence-tiers">
        <h2>2. Evidence Tier Hierarchy (E0–E3)</h2>
        <p>
          To maintain radical transparency and eliminate benchmark inflation, every quantitative score and map projection 
          in Symnoesis must carry a verified evidence tier badge:
        </p>
        <div class="tier-def-list">
          <div class="tier-def-item">
            <span class="badge-tier e0">E0 SPECIFIED</span>
            <p>Expert-elicited prior distributions and mathematical specification. Uncalibrated against real-world outcome telemetry.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tier-def-item">
            <span class="badge-tier e1">E1 SYNTHETIC</span>
            <p>Fully reproducible computational sweeps using mathematically modeled synthetic personas and dyads (spec §12).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tier-def-item">
            <span class="badge-tier e2">E2 PROVISIONAL</span>
            <p>Empirical pilot studies conducted with small volunteer cohorts under informed consent. Unaudited field telemetry.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tier-def-item">
            <span class="badge-tier e3">E3 VALIDATED</span>
            <p>Large-scale, multi-site, preregistered, and independently audited empirical field studies with verified run manifests.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="prior-art">
        <h2>3. Verified Academic Prior Art</h2>
        <p>
          The SYMN-01 framework builds upon validated foundations across cognitive ergonomics, human–computer interaction, 
          and AI safety:
        </p>
        <ul class="citation-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Bainbridge, L. (1983).</strong> "Ironies of Automation." <em>Automatica</em>, 19(6), 775–779. 
            <span class="doi-link"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0005-1098(83)90046-8" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1016/0005-1098(83)90046-8</a></span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Parasuraman, R., Sheridan, T. B., & Wickens, C. D. (2000).</strong> "A model for types and levels of human interaction with automation." 
            <em>IEEE Transactions on Systems, Man, and Cybernetics</em>, 30(3), 286–297.
            <span class="doi-link"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/3468.844354" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1109/3468.844354</a></span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Licklider, J. C. R. (1960).</strong> "Man-Computer Symbiosis." <em>IRE Transactions on Human Factors in Electronics</em>, HFE-1, 4–11.
            <span class="doi-link"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/THFE2.1960.4503259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1109/THFE2.1960.4503259</a></span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="citation">
        <h2>4. How to Cite Symnoesis</h2>
        <p>If you use the Symnoesis specification, Python library, or map tools in academic research, please cite:</p>
        <div class="code-box">
          <pre><code>{`@techreport{symnoesis2026,
  title       = {The Dyadic State: A Framework for Measuring Long-Term Human--Machine Interaction},
  author      = {{Symnoesis Research Initiative}},
  institution = {HarVa Groups},
  year        = {2026},
  number      = {SYMN-01-v0.1.0},
  url         = {https://symnoesis.org}
}`}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</AcademicLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrapper {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .page-lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose-content {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .prose-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .paper-download-card {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .paper-download-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem 0;
  }

  .paper-download-card p {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .paper-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .tier-def-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .tier-def-item {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .tier-def-item p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .citation-list {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .citation-list li {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .doi-link {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .code-box {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .code-box pre {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
</style>
